coder › Implemented `parseMoney(text)` in `src/money.ts`, added tests in `src/money.test.ts`.

What changed:
- `src/money.ts`: detects exactly one currency (`€`/EUR, `$`/USD, `£`/GBP, case-insensitive, anywhere in text); extracts the single digit run (allowing `,`, `.`, space grouping); treats a trailing `,`/`.` + exactly two digits as decimals, all other separators as grouping; negates on leading `-`, `-` after the currency sign/code, or `(…)` around the amount; throws `TypeError` naming the text when currency is missing/unknown/ambiguous or no digits are present.
- `src/money.test.ts`: 6 tests covering the two spec examples, symbols/codes in any position, comma/dot/space grouping, minus/parentheses negatives, and `TypeError`-with-text for bad currency and digit-less input.

Decisions not in the spec:
- Two different currencies in one text (e.g. `€ $10`) also throws `TypeError`, since no single currency can be read.
- `-0` is normalized to `0` cents.
- Codes match with letter boundaries, so `NEURO 100` does not read as EUR.
- One space-separated digit run counts as one amount; two separate amounts throw `TypeError`.

